export const TEMPLATE10_MANDATE_TEXT: string = "# Strategy #10 Mandate — Polydash Yield Fund\n\nStrategy #10 is published on the live StrategyTemplate contract\n(`0xb2a958a9779e02764de006c8aeebc36174e2e3ba`) and is readable by the\nV3 tokenized fund factory. The mandate text below is the\ntemplate's `mandateUri` document (to be pinned to IPFS; the published\n`mandateUri` is the resulting `ipfs://` CID).\n\n## Mandate\n\n> The Polydash Yield Fund earns yield on POLYDASH with ETH subscriptions.\n> It buys POLYDASH, adds POLYDASH/WETH liquidity to earn trading fees, and\n> stakes POLYDASH in Polypad staking pools to earn staking rewards.\n> Harvested trading fees and staking rewards are reinvested — compounded —\n> into more POLYDASH and more liquidity, instead of being paid out as\n> dividends. That compounding is what makes this strategy different from\n> Strategy #6 (LP-Dividend), which pays harvested fees out to holders.\n> Buys are executed in small tranches, each no more than 10% of NAV, paced\n> across days, never chasing a spike. The fund does not sell POLYDASH\n> except to rebalance back to the 80% cap or to pay in-kind exits.\n> Un-deployed ETH stays in WETH in the vault, visible on the public NAV\n> tape. The manager's performance fee is 5% of new gains above the\n> high-water mark only. No leverage, no shorting, no assets outside WETH\n> and POLYDASH.\n\n## Template parameters (as published)\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Assets | `[POLYDASH]` (WETH is the quote asset and is always in the mandate implicitly — the factory rejects WETH in the template list) |\n| Max position | 8000 bps (80% of NAV in POLYDASH) |\n| Max trade | 1000 bps (10% of NAV per trade) |\n| Max deviation | 500 bps (5% vs TWAP feed) |\n| HWM performance fee | 500 bps (5% of new gains only) |\n| Max drawdown | 2000 bps (20% NAV drop pauses new buys) |\n| Skin lock | 2592000 s (30 days) |\n\n## Yield rules\n\n- Pair: POLYDASH/WETH on Uniswap V4.\n- At most 50% of the tokenized fund may sit in liquidity for one pool (LP cap).\n- Every new liquidity position is published first and waits 2 days in public before the manager can add it. Anyone can see it during the wait.\n- The manager may stake POLYDASH in Polypad staking pools to earn staking rewards.\n- Harvested trading fees and staking rewards are reinvested into more POLYDASH and more liquidity (compounding). They are not paid out as dividends.\n- Trading fees in this pool are thin today: about $1.58 per week in total pool fees, shared by every liquidity provider. Yield is not guaranteed and can be near zero.\n- When you exit, you are paid from liquid holdings only. Money in liquidity or staking is paid out only after the manager removes or unstakes it.\n\n## Fund terms (Season 1, as proposed — confirm before creating the fund)\n\n- Mint price 0.01 ETH, raise cap 2 ETH (200 shares), manager skin 5%\n  (10 shares, 0.1 ETH) bought before public mint, entry fee 0%.\n- Exits in-kind (pro-rata POLYDASH + WETH).\n\n## Publish checklist\n\n- [ ] Pin this document to IPFS; record the CID as `mandateUri`.\n- [ ] `publish(mandateHash, mandateUri, [POLYDASH], 8000, 1000, 500, 500, 2000, 2592000)` on StrategyTemplate (owner tx — needs the deployer key).\n- [ ] Verify `templateCount` incremented to 10 and `getTemplate(10)` reads back the params above.\n- [ ] Add Strategy #10 to the create flow (V3 factory routing + name) so it appears as a choice.\n- [ ] Note: POLYDASH is allowlisted (executed Nov 12, 2026) and the TWAP feed\n      is returning prices (poke keeper live since 2026-11-10 ~07:31 PST).\n";
